&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A 90 minute workshop for Columbia faculty.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;How can we prepare students to engage constructively across diverse perspectives and backgrounds? This interactive workshop invites faculty to explore pedagogies of pluralism through a &amp;ldquo;Respect, Relate, Cooperate&amp;rdquo; framework as a practical lens for fostering connection and collaboration across a variety of worldviews and experiences. Participants will practice bridge-building strategies that strengthen classroom dialogue and consider classroom strategies that cultivate curiosity, empathy, and shared learning purpose among students.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Session objectives:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By the end of this session, participants will be able to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Explain how the respect-relate-cooperate framework can inform classroom practices that support engagement across diverse perspectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Apply at least one bridge-building strategy to foster pluralism in their own teaching context.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
